{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545276-aggravated-damage-lethal","id":1545276,"title":"Aggravated Damage & Lethal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-03T21:29:16-08:00","id":1545276,"title":"Aggravated Damage & Lethal","content":"So, in Dark Ages: Vampire, mortals can't soak lethal-damage with their stamina, only with armor, well, isn't lethal-damage now equal to aggravated-damage? So, what's the point of having agg-claws or a magic-sword that does aggravated-damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T23:29:00-08:00","id":1545279,"title":"","content":"Agg isn't meant to be used on humans. It's meant to be used on beings that can heal quickly, because it keeps them from doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T04:34:52-08:00","id":1545303,"title":"","content":"Generally, yeah, for normal humans lethal and agg are the same thing.<br /> <br /> That said, on top of it not being the same thing for supernaturals, that also applies to supernaturals that want to heal a human. If you're trying to kill a squishy mortal ally of a supernatural enemy, it is frequently the case that using agg means that even if you fail to kill them, it's much harder for your supernatural foe to help them recover from the injury compared to lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T18:08:28-08:00","id":1545356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1545276-aggravated-damage-lethal#post1545276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in Dark Ages: Vampire, mortals can't soak lethal-damage with their stamina, only with armor, well, isn't lethal-damage now equal to aggravated-damage? So, what's the point of having agg-claws or a magic-sword that does aggravated-damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically the same type of damage. It kills just the same. Being impaled by a spear with &quot;only lethal, normal&quot; damage or one that deals aggravated damage will kill you just the same.<br /> <br /> The difference exists merely for the many critters of the night that can actually soak up that sort of damage - a spear on a vampire or a werewolf would probably just break without hurting them. And it also prevents these critters from using their supernatural super fast self healing traits. That's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}